{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"WAVE 1 - VERDICT. rebar is NOT categorically worse. It contributes 61 TPs no other arm found across 23 criteria; it has the second-best severity honesty (6% vs CE's 27%), which matters disproportionately for something that gates; it was the only arm to examine security at all (a live PAT-in-logs path on bda8, judged understated rather than overstated); and it is the only arm that is a GATE rather than a document - a signed attestation pinned to a code SHA and material fingerprint that blocks the claim. Its raw numbers are also depressed by the prior-review confound described above. The honest summary: CE for recall, superpowers for signal-to-noise, mini for out-of-tree factual grounding, rebar for gating. The configuration the data supports is running both rebar (gating) and a finder (advisory), not choosing one."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789000852819373001,"uuid":"2a6eeafb-f0ac-407a-b801-35ce4655d009"}